  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investing in Wildlife Conservation through Enforcement, Livelihoods and Tourism (WildINVEST)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: Disbursement data provided is cumulative and covers disbursement made by the project Agency.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The WildINVEST Challenge grant initiative will aim to generate direct benefits to local communities, including IPs, in and around protected areas, buffer zones, KBAs etc. The focus will be on supporting biodiversity-friendly enterprises with some links to eco-tourism.  This is explained in the project approach. (Note a Small Grants Specialist will support this process)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To disrupt illegal wildlife trade and protect biodiversity by investing in law enforcement and judicial capacity, eco-tourism and wildlife-based economies, and protected area management for sustained environmental benefits and human well-being</narrative>
  </description>
